{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antiviral, Antiparasitic, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (53.3%) to Ponericin W5. Activity: Active against Gram+ bacteria S. aureus ATCC 25923, E. faecalis ATCC 29212, S. epidermidis ATCC 12228, E. casseliflavus ATCC 700327 (MIC 4-8 uM). Gram- E. coli ATCC 25922, K. pneumoniae ATCC 13883 (MIC 8 uM), K. pneumoniae carbapanemase (KPC) MR, P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 (MIC 16-32 uM). Antiparasitic against Trypanosoma epimastigotes form T. cruzi (MIC 6.3 uM). The peptide also inhibits cancer cell proliferation (IC50 = 12.8 uM for B16F10 murine melanoma cells and IC50= 15.3 uM for MCF-7 human breast cancer cells) in a dose-dependent manner. The peptide is also antiviral against CHIKV (EC50 =17 uM), DENV4 (EC50 20.8 uM), and YFV (EC50=21.8 uM). not toxic to noninfected Huh7 cells at 25 uM. In vitro Toxicity: It is moderate hemolytic HC50 49 uM (cf. mellitin HC50 5 uM). Structure: Helical in 50% TFE. Peptide engineering: To imporve peptide stability, stapled peptides have been designed (e.g., F2-12) based on this sequence ( Xue et al., 2024). Updated Jan2024", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "32443921", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Biomolecules. 2020;10(5):E790. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03190", "source_id": "AP03190", "source_numeric_id": "03190", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03190", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Biological Properties of a Novel Multifunctional Host Defense Peptide From the Skin Secretion of the Chaco Tree Frog, Boana raniceps", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
